<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; Man and Sin" cic="CCC 355-421" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does it mean that the human being was created &laquo;in the image of God&raquo;? What capacities make us his image?</li>
<li>What does Genesis say about the unity of body and soul in the human being?</li>
<li>What was the first sin and what did it really consist of?</li>
<li>What is concupiscence and how is it related to original sin?</li>
<li>What is the &laquo;Protoevangelium&raquo; and where is it found in the Bible?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Saint Augustine says: &laquo;I was made and I unmade myself.&raquo; In what areas of your life do you feel that God's image is wounded? Where do you notice that tension between what you want to do and what you end up doing?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think of Paul's words: &laquo;I do not do what I want, but I do the very thing I hate&raquo; (Rom 7:15). Does that sound familiar?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. The serpent tempted Eve by distorting God's word. What &laquo;serpents&raquo; whisper to you today that God does not love you or that his commandments are oppressive?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">It could be a person, a culture, an inner voice. Name it honestly.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Imagine you are Adam or Eve right after eating the fruit. What do you feel? What would you say to God if he came looking for you in that moment?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Remember: God did not destroy them. He sought them out and made them a promise.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Compare Genesis 3 with the Annunciation (Lk 1:26-38). In the garden, a woman says &laquo;no&raquo; and sin enters. In Nazareth, a woman says &laquo;yes&raquo; and salvation enters. What does this connection say to you?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Mary is called &laquo;the new Eve.&raquo; How does she respond differently to God's invitation?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. In what areas of your life do you need Christ to &laquo;crush the serpent's head&raquo;? What wound do you want him to heal?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Name something concrete. You don't have to share it with anyone but God.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Read Genesis 3:1-15 aloud</h4>
<p>After reading, identify: what did God actually say? What did the serpent say? How did the serpent distort God's word? Write down the differences you find.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Write a letter to God about your sin</h4>
<p>Begin with &laquo;Lord, I hid myself because...&raquo; and write honestly. Not to condemn yourself, but to recognize that he is already seeking you, just as he sought Adam in the garden.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Drawing the broken mirror</h4>
<p>The image of God in us is like a broken mirror: the pieces still reflect the light, but the image is distorted. Draw a broken mirror and write on each fragment something that still reflects God's image in you (capacity to love, create, forgive...). Then write on the cracks what you need Christ to heal.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;Where sin increased, grace abounded all the more.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; Romans 5:20</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord, you who created me in your image<br />
and seek me even when I hide,<br />
have mercy on my frailty.<br />
I confess that I sometimes choose my own will<br />
over your love.<br />
But I believe that your grace is greater than my sin.<br />
May Mary, the new Eve,<br />
teach me to say &laquo;yes&raquo; where I have said &laquo;no.&raquo;<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

